144 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The gaze functions here not as an act of perception but as a regime of existence. It binds the subject to visibility while concealing its own authority. To gaze is to claim the right to define; to be gazed upon is to be fixed within that claim. Between these poles, the subject emerges as both ruler and captive, sustained by the illusion that autonomy can be wrested from the very system that produces it.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
