/T (Originally conceived by philosopher Jeremy Bentham and rendered by architect Willey Reveley, this architectural drawing visualizes a model of total surveillance: a circular prison with a central observation tower from which one guard can watch all inmates without being seen. The structure transforms visibility into discipline, operating through the anticipation of observation.)
/E (Originally conceived by philosopher Jeremy Bentham and rendered by architect Willey Reveley, this architectural drawing visualizes a model of total surveillance: a circular prison with a central observation tower from which one guard can watch all inmates without being seen. The structure transforms visibility into discipline, operating through the anticipation of observation.)
