171 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (More than a dozen security cameras are attached to the edges of ocean rocks, each pointing in a different direction toward the surrounding environment. Geltner assembles clusters of technological and surveillance devices in public spaces, drawing attention to the saturation of monitoring systems in contemporary life.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
172 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (This iteration displaces these devices into a natural landscape, where their abrupt presence disrupts expectations of safety and neutrality. By inserting the logic of surveillance into nature, the work exposes how deeply embedded monitoring has become in both urban and non-urban environments.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
